[2026/05/15 21:36:56] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_N6GTWgU4O1GijQfJulU6OhLb', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"I will build a compact experimental pipeline in LensKit 0.14.4 that loads the three provided implicit-feedback datasets, applies 5-core filtering, and binarizes MovieLens and Amazon interactions using a rating threshold greater than 3. For each dataset, I will generate five fixed random seeds and perform a user-based 80/20 holdout split so every user contributes interactions to both train and test when possible. I will train three standard baselines—ALS, ItemKNN, and Pop—using LensKit implementations with simple default-style hyperparameters suitable for implicit recommendation. Evaluation will compute Precision@1,5,10 and nDCG@1,5,10 from top-N recommendations while excluding training items from candidate sets. I will aggregate results across seeds into a tidy table and print per-run metrics as well as mean and standard deviation by dataset and algorithm. For a short statistical analysis, I will run paired comparisons across seeds between algorithms within each dataset using simple paired t-tests on nDCG@10 and Precision@10, while also reporting the variability attributable to split seeds. To satisfy reproducibility and artifact requirements, the script will save all collected metrics and summary arrays under the working directory and generate a small visualization of score variability across seeds. The implementation is intentionally straightforward and self-contained so it can serve as a solid baseline before exploring more advanced protocol changes or hyperparameter tuning.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport warnings\\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom scipy.stats import ttest_rel\\n\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms import Recommender\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\\n\\nexperiment_data = {\\n    \'ml100k\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n    \'amazon_videogames\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n    \'lastfm\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n}\\n\\nSEEDS = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84]\\nKS = [1, 5, 10]\\n\\n\\ndef load_ml100k(path=\'u.data\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\', names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n    return df\\n\\n\\ndef load_amazon(path=\'VideoGames.csv\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, header=None, names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n    return df\\n\\n\\ndef load_lastfm(path=\'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\')\\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n    user_col = cols[[c for c in cols if \'user\' in c][0]]\\n    item_candidates = [c for c in cols if \'artist\' in c]\\n    item_col = cols[item_candidates[0]]\\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].copy()\\n    df.columns = [\'user\', \'item\']\\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\\n    df = df.drop_duplicates([\'user\', \'item\'])\\n    return df\\n\\n\\ndef k_core_filter(df, min_user=5, min_item=5):\\n    out = df.copy()\\n    changed = True\\n    while changed:\\n        before = len(out)\\n        uc = out.groupby(\'user\').size()\\n        out = out[out[\'user\'].isin(uc[uc >= min_user].index)]\\n        ic = out.groupby(\'item\').size()\\n        out = out[out[\'item\'].isin(ic[ic >= min_item].index)]\\n        changed = len(out) != before\\n    return out.reset_index(drop=True)\\n\\n\\ndef user_holdout(df, test_ratio=0.2, seed=42):\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n    train_parts, test_parts = [], []\\n    for _, grp in df.groupby(\'user\'):\\n        grp = grp.sample(frac=1, random_state=int(rng.integers(1_000_000_000)))\\n        n = len(grp)\\n        n_test = max(1, int(np.floor(n * test_ratio))) if n >= 2 else 0\\n        if n_test >= n:\\n            n_test = n - 1\\n        test = grp.iloc[:n_test]\\n        train = grp.iloc[n_test:]\\n        if len(train) > 0:\\n            train_parts.append(train)\\n        if len(test) > 0:\\n            test_parts.append(test)\\n    train = pd.concat(train_parts, ignore_index=True)\\n    test = pd.concat(test_parts, ignore_index=True)\\n    return train, test\\n\\n\\ndef precision_at_k(recs, truth, k):\\n    if len(recs) == 0:\\n        return 0.0\\n    topk = recs[:k]\\n    hits = sum(1 for x in topk if x in truth)\\n    return hits / k\\n\\n\\ndef ndcg_at_k(recs, truth, k):\\n    topk = recs[:k]\\n    dcg = 0.0\\n    for i, item in enumerate(topk, start=1):\\n        if item in truth:\\n            dcg += 1.0 / np.log2(i + 1)\\n    ideal_hits = min(len(truth), k)\\n    if ideal_hits == 0:\\n        return 0.0\\n    idcg = sum(1.0 / np.log2(i + 1) for i in range(1, ideal_hits + 1))\\n    return dcg / idcg\\n\\n\\ndef eval_algo(algo, train, test, name, ds_name, seed):\\n    model = Recommender.adapt(algo)\\n    model.fit(train)\\n    truth = test.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(set).to_dict()\\n    users = sorted(set(train[\'user\']).intersection(truth.keys()))\\n    rows = []\\n    for user in users:\\n        try:\\n        