[2026/05/15 21:38:35] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an experienced recommender systems researcher. Your previous code for research experiment had a bug, so based on the information below, you should revise it in order to fix this bug. Your response should be an implementation outline in natural language, followed by a single markdown code block which implements the bugfix/solution.', 'Research task': ' You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI’d like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS,\nItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback:\nMovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your\nworking directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon\nand MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit\ninteractions. Here’s the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random\nseeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based\n80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a\nshort statistical analysis.', 'Previous (buggy) implementation': '```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom scipy.stats import ttest_rel\n\nfrom lenskit.algorithms import Recommender\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    \'ml100k\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\n    \'amazon_videogames\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\n    \'lastfm\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\n}\n\nSEEDS = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84]\nKS = [1, 5, 10]\n\n\ndef load_ml100k(path=\'u.data\'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\t\', names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\n    return df\n\n\ndef load_amazon(path=\'VideoGames.csv\'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, header=None, names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\n    return df\n\n\ndef load_lastfm(path=\'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat\'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\t\')\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = cols[[c for c in cols if \'user\' in c][0]]\n    item_candidates = [c for c in cols if \'artist\' in c]\n    item_col = cols[item_candidates[0]]\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].copy()\n    df.columns = [\'user\', \'item\']\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\n    df = df.drop_duplicates([\'user\', \'item\'])\n    return df\n\n\ndef k_core_filter(df, min_user=5, min_item=5):\n    out = df.copy()\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        before = len(out)\n        uc = out.groupby(\'user\').size()\n        out = out[out[\'user\'].isin(uc[uc >= min_user].index)]\n        ic = out.groupby(\'item\').size()\n        out = out[out[\'item\'].isin(ic[ic >= min_item].index)]\n        changed = len(out) != before\n    return out.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n\ndef user_holdout(df, test_ratio=0.2, seed=42):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    train_parts, test_parts = [], []\n    for _, grp in df.groupby(\'user\'):\n        grp = grp.sample(frac=1, random_state=int(rng.integers(1_000_000_000)))\n        n = len(grp)\n        n_test = max(1, int(np.floor(n * test_ratio))) if n >= 2 else 0\n        if n_test >= n:\n            n_test = n - 1\n        test = grp.iloc[:n_test]\n        train = grp.iloc[n_test:]\n        if len(train) > 0:\n            train_parts.append(train)\n        if len(test) > 0:\n            test_parts.append(test)\n    train = pd.concat(train_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    test = pd.concat(test_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    return train, test\n\n\ndef precision_at_k(recs, truth, k):\n    if len(recs) == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    topk = recs[:k]\n    hits = sum(1 for x in topk if x in truth)\n    return hits / k\n\n\ndef ndcg_at_k(recs, truth, k):\n    topk = recs[:k]\n    dcg = 0.0\n    for i, item in enumerate(topk, start=1):\n        if item in truth:\n            dcg += 1.0 / np.log2(i + 1)\n    ideal_hits = min(len(truth), k)\n    if ideal_hits == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    idcg = sum(1.0 / np.log2(i + 1) for i in range(1, ideal_hits + 1))\n    return dcg / idcg\n\n\ndef eval_algo(algo, train, test, name, ds_name, seed):\n    model = Recommender.adapt(algo)\n    model.fit(train)\n    truth = test.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(set).to_dict()\n    users = sorted(set(train[\'user\']).intersection(truth.keys()))\n    rows = []\n    for user in users:\n        try:\n            recs = model.recommend(user, 10)\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        if recs is None or len(recs) == 0:\n            rec_items = []\n        else:\n            rec_items = recs[\'item\'].tolist()\n        gt = truth[user]\n        row = {\'dataset\': ds_